The word "begin", at the left margin is erroneously interpreted by OE
as introducing a UUENCODEd attachment.  (Or so I confidently assume)

The supposed attachment ends with the word "end" at the left margin.

This behavior originates in the days before MIME when the standard
way of incorporating binary attachments within a text message was
to UUENCODE the attachment and embed it within the text.

